SUMMARY: Fashion Art Toronto Open Air
DESCRIPTION:Fashion Art Toronto Open Air\n\nMay 26\, 2026\n5PM–9PM\n\n...
 .\n\nFree Public Event\nReserved Seating Available Online\n\nTickets: Fas
 hionarttoronto.ca https://www.fashionarttoronto.ca/\n\n....\n\nFashion Ar
 t Toronto presents its Open Air Fashion Week edition as part of its city-
 wide Fashion Week programming on Tuesday\, May 26 with a large-scale outd
 oor runway event at The Distillery Historic District in Toronto.\n\nSet a
 gainst the iconic cobblestone streets and industrial architecture of one 
 of the city’s most celebrated cultural destinations\, the evening brings 
 together fashion\, performance\, music\, and community in an immersive op
 en-air experience.\n\nThe event is free and open to the public. Limited r
 unway seating is ticketed. Guests are invited to explore the Distillery D
 istrict while enjoying music\, fashion\, and cultural programming through
 out the evening.\n\n....\n\n\nSCHEDULE OF EVENTS:\n\n6PM — Live Performan
 ce by Sara Kae\n\n6PM —Runway Show\n\nAyimach Horizons — Rainbow\, Illumi
 nosity and the Dream\n\n7PM — Performance by House of Marylin Monroe\n\n7
 PM — Runway Show\nLignes de Fuite Presents\nLeidy beibi / Charlize Therri
 en / Tiina Sarajev / Jejune\n\n8PM — Live Performance by Natasha Fisher\n
 \n8PM — Runway Show\nWABANOONKWE — Nocturnal Rose\n\n....\n\n\nABOUT THE 
 DESIGNERS\n\nAyimach Horizons is the fashion practice of Cree-Métis artis
 t and designer Jason Baerg. Blending Indigenous futurism\, ecological con
 sciousness\, and multidisciplinary art practice\, Rainbow\, Illuminosity 
 and the Dream explores the relationship between land\, identity\, light\,
  and imagined futures through a series of interconnected colour worlds an
 d sculptural garments.\n\nLignes de Fuite is a Montreal-based fashion inc
 ubator showcasing a curated runway presentation spotlighting a new genera
 tion of experimental French-Canadian designers pushing the boundaries of 
 fashion\, identity\, and performance. The showcase brings together four d
 istinct voices exploring themes of transformation\, power\, reconstructio
 n\, and contemporary culture through avant-garde silhouette\, styling\, a
 nd material experimentation.\n\n\nWABANOONKWE is an Indigenous woman-owne
 d fashion house led by Anishinaabe designer Wabanoonkwe. Her couture coll
 ection Nocturnal Rose merges romance\, femininity\, and mystery through s
 culpted floral forms\, tailored silhouettes\, velvet\, and liquid satin —
  creating a cinematic runway experience rooted in Indigenous storytelling
  and contemporary elegance.\n\n....\n\n\nABOUT FASHION ART TORONTO\n\nFas
 hion Art Toronto takes place city-wide May 25–31\, 2026\, transforming To
 ronto into a dynamic hub of fashion\, art\, retail\, nightlife\, and perf
 ormance. Under this season’s theme\, “Toronto\, Show Yourself\,” the fest
 ival brings together more than 50 Canadian designers and artists across r
 unway presentations\, installations\, immersive experiences\, and cultura
 l activations throughout the city — positioning Toronto on the global fas
 hion stage.\n\n
