SUMMARY: Movie Night @ Soulpepper: Really Happy Someday
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Soulpepper Theatre for a screening of Really Happy
  Someday\, an indie drama set firmly in Toronto\, featuring beloved local
  actors.\n\nBefore he transitioned\, Z (Breton Lalama) was a rising music
 al theatre star struggling with his gender identity. One year into taking
  testosterone\, he has finally started to feel at home in his body but ha
 s lost all control of his voice. At the same time\, Z’s long-term partner
 \, Danielle (Khadijah Roberts-Abdullah)\, feels she’s lost the person she
  fell in love with. Unable to book work with his changing voice\, Z start
 s bartending where his new boss\, Santi\, emboldens him to fight for hims
 elf and his dreams. Z starts working with a singing instructor\, Shelly\,
  to learn how to use his new voice\, and maybe even trust himself.\n\nSti
 ck around after the screening for a conversation between star and co-writ
 er Breton Lalama and Soulpepper's Artistic Director Paolo Santalucia.\n\n
 Free general admission. More info and tickets here https://www.soulpepper
 .ca/public-domain/whats-on/reallyhappysomeday .
CATEGORIES:free,movie,film,LGBTQ
